WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Imagine the leanest plant in America.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.080
Robots run all night.

3
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.730
Every dollar of waste has been cut.

4
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.460
Each unit it makes costs as
little as it possibly could.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.470
Its managers say it is
perfectly efficient.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:15.670
Are they right?

7
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.060
Can a firm make goods
at the lowest possible

8
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.940
cost and still waste resources?

9
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.710
In this mission, you'll find
the output where average

10
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.990
total cost is lowest,
from a table of costs.

11
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.490
Then you'll move a
market price up and down

12
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.310
and see when a firm is truly efficient.

13
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.520
Your mission: find out what
economists really mean by efficient.
